#include "globals.h"

extern char D_800118E4[]; /* GPU debug tag */
extern int D_80074B20;    /* OT terminator sentinel */

/* Reset an ordering table to empty (0x8005fc6c): optionally trace, hand the
   table to the +0x2C command-table method, then write the terminator link
   into the head entry. Returns the table. */
int *func_8005FC6C(int *ot, int n) {
  if (g_bGpuDebugLevel >= 2) {
    ((void (*)(char *, int *, int))g_pfnGpuDebugPrintf)(D_800118E4, ot, n);
  }
  (*(void (**)(int *, int))((char *)g_pGpuDispatchTable + 0x2C))(ot, n);
  *ot = 0xFFFFFF & (int)&D_80074B20;
  return ot;
}

/* PARKED at 7/38 (length-exact; was the 2026-07-06 "F4 return-pointer
   coalescing" park, re-derived 2026-08-10-2, refined 2026-08-10-3 — the body
   above is correct and the whole debug/dispatch head matches).

   Refinement 2026-08-10-3: writing the mask on the LEFT
   (`0xFFFFFF & (int)&D_80074B20`, A106/A178) is what puts the `li` of the mask
   BEFORE the `la` of the symbol, which is the original's order. Keep it.

   Residue (F4): the original materialises the `return ot` copy BEFORE the
   terminator computation (`move v0,s0` sits between the mask `li` and the
   symbol `la`), so v0 is occupied, the mask/symbol fall to a0/v1 and cse
   re-bases the store on the copy (`sw v1,0(v0)`). Ours emits `move v0,s0`
   after the store and stores through s0.
   Mechanism: the three tail insns (mask li, ret copy, symbol la) are all
   dep-free priority-1 stragglers, so A164 says their order IS source order —
   the original's source evaluates the return value between the mask and the
   symbol. But every C form that would emit that copy gets it propagated away:
   `int *head = ot;` before the store, after the store, storing through `ot` vs
   through `head`, `ot[0]` + `return &ot[0]`, and a named mask local all give
   the identical byte (re-tested 2026-08-10-3 with the mask-first form). A171's
   "dies last" dial does not apply either — copy propagation removes the copy
   before cse ever builds the equivalence.
   Also tried 2026-08-10-3 and rejected: duplicating the whole tail in both
   arms of the debug `if` to manufacture A151's two-exit hoist — jump.c does
   NOT cross-jump the two copies back (+7 insns, slot overflow).
   MECHANISM NAILED 2026-08-11-1 (read off cse.c `make_regs_eqv`): for a copy
   `head = ot`, the DEST only becomes cse's canonical reg when
   `(last_use(head) > cse_basic_block_end || first_use(head) < cse_bb_start)`
   AND `last_use(head) > last_use(ot)`. In a straight-line TAIL block the first
   clause is false — the ebb runs to the end of the function — so `ot` stays
   canonical, every use of `head` is rewritten back to `ot`, and the copy dies.
   The clause is only satisfiable when the copy sits inside a CONDITIONAL ARM
   and its uses are past the join (that is exactly how the same class was
   solved in UpdateGemPickupPathCamera, 2026-08-11-1 — see A187). This tail has
   no branch after the dispatch call, so the lever cannot be aimed here.
   `int *mask/head` locals ordered [mask li, copy, symbol la] re-tested
   2026-08-11-1: byte-identical, as predicted by the rule above.

   2026-08-14-1 unattended permuter session (~15m, ~116400 iterations -- the
   highest count of the session, this being a 38-insn function, timed out at the
   15m budget): best score 95 vs first-iteration score 115, with the next
   candidate at 100. A very flat curve over a very large sample, which supports
   the analysis above: the A187 lever is genuinely unaimable here (no branch
   after the dispatch call), so random permutation has nothing to find. Treat as
   settled for unattended runs. Still PARKED (see above). */
